WEBVTT

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:30.700
You

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:31.230
Thank you.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:07.640
Come on.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:09.120
Aren't you going to report in?

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:11.920
Shall I make it?

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:15.110
Oh, go ahead.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:15.940
All right.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.060
This is area A.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.280
Stand by, I'm going to report on unit number three.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.510
Let me know as soon as you are recording.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.290
This is base unit. Go ahead, inspection team.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:39.950
It's exactly...

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:40.700
8.38.

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:43.470
Temperature and humidity.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.280
The same as Unit 6.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.540
Battery charged to full capacity, voltage stable.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:49.900
Silver iodide's okay.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:50.200
Morial?

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:52.020
That's not a proper report.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:57.610
Each inspector.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:59.480
must be a thoroughly detailed confirmation.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.240
I will decide what is the same and what is okay.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:02.580
Right.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:03.270
So is that.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:10.760
Uh-huh.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:14.630
He's a stickler.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.980
I don't like that, Doctor. He's not the only thing I don't like around here.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.040
Huh.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.500
The island's much too hot.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:24.850
The heat makes it hard even to think.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:26.230
Thank you.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:29.400
things off again.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:31.440
I'll be ready in case it sees us.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:37.960
again

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.340
When we get off this island, the better I like it.

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:07.750
You said there was something wrong with the high-altitude component, right?

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:08.490
Uh-huh.

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:09.090
What's wrong?

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.020
Printed circuit has a break.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.420
Then change the component.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.130
The experiment's too important.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.430
I want everything to work right.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:16.540
Yes, sir.

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:22.750
I don't know why I agreed to come to this island.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:24.110
You volunteered, I thought.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:25.360
That's right.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:29.920
I figured there's a lot I could learn working for a famous scientist like Dr. Kosumi.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.230
And actually, it's turned out even better than I expected.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:33.990
So, why complain, eh?

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.970
Well, the only trouble is, he keeps us on our toes, day and night.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.930
He's got us going 24 hours a day.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:42.180
I get homesick once in a while for an ice-cold glass of beer.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.110
I know what you mean. Thanks, Ozawa.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:51.050
There's some interference.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.970
Huh? It's happening again.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:56.430
Get a bearing and hurry.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:57.100
Okay.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.260
That's the end of the interference.

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:03.480
Were you able to get a fix on it?

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.010
South? Southwest?

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.340
It's strange. I just can't figure it out.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:09.820
Something's causing it. But what?

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:11.910
I wish I knew the answer.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.540
Oh, what is it?

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:33.580
Who are we? We're going to have visitors.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:36.360
It's impossible. Nobody's supposed to know that we're here.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.910
The project's known only to the United Nations Commission on Agriculture.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.880
You're right. Then the United Nations must have sent it.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:06.560
Nice of you to come and meet me.

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:11.280
I don't have a lot to carry, just my luggage,

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:12.970
but I'll take care of it myself.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:15.880
Who are you, huh?

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:20.410
Maki Goro's the name, a reporter and photographer.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:22.680
You'll have to go home.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:24.540
I'm sorry, but I won't go.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:25.890
I can't permit you to stay.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.620
No, I want the story and I'm staying till I get it.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:29.340
I will not go home.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:32.540
There isn't any story.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:58.160
Sit there forever.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:06:58.780
Right.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:04.210
You can't stay on the island. We don't want any publicity at all at this time.

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:06.070
I didn't come here to do publicity.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:10.090
Just dropped in after I felt a pain in my stomach.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:12.100
Oh, you did, eh?

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:12.850
That's right.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:17.170
You see, whenever I think there's a good story, I get this sort of ache.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.230
And my stomach doesn't lie. That's how I know I'm onto a good story.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.000
And I'm staying right here till I get it.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.210
Now, isn't it the same with you?

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:29.970
You start out making tests, and you don't stop till you...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:38.130
get what you want. You're being smart, too smart. You know, sir, I guess he'll have to stay. There's

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:42.730
no way to send him back. And after all, we are short-handed in this place, doctor. Let's assign

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:47.940
him a little work, eh? I can think of a dozen necessary chores like cleaning and KP and trash

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:53.930
to smoke. Now, wait a minute. It's either that or start swimming home. What do you say, doctor?

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:58.360
Do you plan to leave that life jacket on forever? Huh?

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:07.110
Ah, you're officially accepted. You're now a member here.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.180
You'd better be a good cook, though.

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:23.460
What's that? What's that strange noise?

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:24.720
You're about to find out.

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:27.040
Look, can you see it out there?

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.280
You can't go into the jungle after dark, it's too dangerous.

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:03.970
I didn't get a shot.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:25.160
Mr. Fujisak, were you able to find the giant mantis?

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:29.970
Don't you think you'd better concentrate on making a good deal?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:35.360
for tonight? I, uh, hey, anything interesting happen out there? There's nothing interesting

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:43.800
anywhere on this cursed island. I guess the heat makes him feel like that, huh? Uh-huh. It gets

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:49.260
everybody here. I don't know how much longer any of us will be able to stay here. Why do you say

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:56.320
that? We've all been on this spooky island three months already. Huh, it's interesting. You think

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.600
it's spooky, huh? Oh?

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:02.150
What have you got there?

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:03.740
Just greens to make a salad.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:05.440
But we use that for washing clothes then.

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:08.230
I know. Nobody's been using it today, though.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:09.130
Oh, that's what you think.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.340
Look, Mario washed his clothes in it this morning.

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:20.110
Ah, Goro, what's for dinner?

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.030
We're going to have stewed vegetables again tonight.

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:26.410
Goro's got a new specialty.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.400
Those vegetables look wilted.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:29.790
Why don't you get fresh ones?

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.640
These were the only ones I could find.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:32.800
Try something else.

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:34.160
We call it soul girl spinach.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:38.590
Most of it's been picked from around the camp.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:40.810
You'll find a whole lot of it back in the jungle.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:41.860
Oh, uh-huh.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:06.490
The weather conditions are getting a lot better.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.800
If it continues like this, you can start your testing, sir.

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:12.970
That low-pressure area there could cause us trouble, I think.

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:14.180
I don't think it will, do you?

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:15.200
I'm not sure, sir.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.200
A high-altitude wind should push it to the north,

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:19.670
otherwise it will remain stationary, and that'll be good.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:24.540
Well, in slightly less than 24 hours, our tests can start.

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:27.550
Of course. That's good news. Very good news.

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:29.350
Doctor.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.060
Are you going to try to freeze this island?

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:34.030
Don't ask so many questions.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.260
I can't help worrying what'll happen to that native girl.

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:40.110
What native girl?

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.810
That's ridiculous. It's uninhabited, the entire island.

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.180
Is it? I saw a girl with my own eyes.

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:48.930
You just imagined it. Every part of this island was searched, right?

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:49.750
Yes, all of it is.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.090
But she could have been hiding.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:53.680
Please don't start your test until you get it as safe.

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:54.540
Who cares about her?

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:57.320
It'd mean just one more delay, that's all.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:12:59.970
And all we want to do is...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.920
Get off this silence or let's get the test over with!

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:17.400
Doctor, is the test really that important?

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:23.840
Yes. The result could change the future of everyone in just a short time.

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:29.930
You claim you're a journalist, so you know how quickly the Earth's population is reaching its...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:38.640
Limit, hmm? Yes. Know what children then will face? They'll starve to death. In only a few years,

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:45.050
there won't be enough for anyone. And so our plan is to make use of all the wastelands here on Earth.

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:51.960
The Siberian tundra, the African deserts, South American jungles. At present, they can be used for

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:58.640
very little. And yet, if we can control the weather conditions as well as climate and temperature,

00:13:58.950 --> 00:13:59.890
we'll make fertile lands.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:02.830
Can you really control weather?

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:04.860
Yes, in theory we can.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.160
And that's why we're here, to test that theory.

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:11.850
Let me ask you another question.

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:15.580
If you're working for the good of the world, why keep it secret, huh?

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:16.820
For a good reason.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:21.010
Anyone who knows about it could turn any area on the earth to ice.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:25.260
In the wrong hands, such power could create havoc.

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:29.980
Try to get a good night's sleep.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:31.430
At dawn, we'll start the test.

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:28.710
Clouds, turn 98, 60.

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:35.320
Zero in exactly 20 more minutes.

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:58.920
Zero. All units stand by.

00:15:59.150 --> 00:15:59.830
Where's that newspaper?

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:03.790
Oh, he's somewhere around. He was here five minutes ago, sir.

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:05.440
You'd better sound the alarm.

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:31.320
You don't need to hide!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.860
You've got to get out of this area!

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:50.370
Start the experiment, 10 seconds.

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:59.350
Eight, four, two, one, zero.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:26.010
Refrigeration unit refrigeration units beginning to go up temperature of unit minus 1,200 altitude 300 and it's still climbing steadily 400

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:33.780
Good. Standby to blow dump. Ignite at 800 feet.

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:51.070
Nearing 800. 100.

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:52.120
Blow dump.

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:02.020
An updraft has started, sir.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.620
Throwing the hot air away from the island is expected.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:07.720
Start operating the towers.

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:08.060
Yes, sir.

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:17.440
Eject silver iodide.

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:34.920
Now, where is she?

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:39.410
Temperature has dropped 10 degrees centigrade since the experiment began.

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:41.090
It's working so far, Doctor.

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:42.890
I'd say it's a success.

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:45.040
Has Goro come back yet?

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:46.000
No, sir.

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:47.820
Let's hope he doesn't catch pneumonia out there.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:49.720
Look, the temperature is still dropping.

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:51.310
It's already much colder.

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:51.510
Good.

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:56.250
Cut the system for cooling and start up heating operation.

00:18:57.760 --> 00:18:59.980
Activate the solar heat stage and launch the radioactive unit.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:20.200
The remote control neuron's not working.

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:20.600
It's not.

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:23.990
Doctor, the balloon transmitter doesn't respond.

00:19:24.150 --> 00:19:24.750
It's completely out.

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:25.750
Try another frequency.

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:26.190
What is it?

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:28.940
It seems as though something's jamming the wavelengths.

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:32.390
Can we get the unit down in time?

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:34.200
Sorry, sir. It's impossible.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.040
What'll happen if we can't detonate it correctly?

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:38.310
It'd be a disaster. We've got to try to do it.

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:41.880
Otherwise, the unit will cause intense heat and a radioactive storm.

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:43.670
Haven't you made contact?

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:44.550
No, not yet.

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:58.470
The radioactive capsule created a chain reaction.

00:19:58.990 --> 00:19:59.970
Solgill Island became...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.600
in the center of a radioactive storm.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:04.550
The temperature rose to nearly 200 degrees.

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:19.610
Tremendous heat precipitated a thunderstorm of cloudburst proportions.

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:22.360
and the rain that fell was near the boiling point.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:55.780
side.

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:01.260
Ah, it must.

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:02.810
Good to get outside, isn't it?

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:05.790
You know, with all this heat, I feel as if I'm a roast chicken.

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:08.510
Well, I guess that puts an end on the test.

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:09.500
What?

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:11.010
Oh, I don't think it does.

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:14.550
I began working for the doctor long before coming here.

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:16.990
And the more difficulties he runs into,

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:18.470
The harder he tries.

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:20.210
Setbacks only encourage him.

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:25.830
I have new orders.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.120
You're to look over everything.

00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:33.900
The doctor wants to know exactly what was wrecked.

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:35.660
He intends to go on with the test.

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:38.180
That's what I do. He didn't give up after all.

00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:40.210
There was no reason to be discouraged.

00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:41.810
Now check everything carefully and good luck.

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:04.850
Doctor!

00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:06.240
See those rocks over there?

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:07.420
Yes, we'll have them.

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:09.250
That's where I saw that girl swimming.

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:13.140
I don't think she could have survived in all that heat.

00:22:14.170 --> 00:22:15.810
You still don't believe I really saw a girl?

00:22:16.440 --> 00:22:18.060
Not at all, and I don't believe in ghosts either.

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:34.280
Doctor?

00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:36.860
It's gotten bigger. How did it grow so large?

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:40.140
The intense heat and the radioactive storm did it.

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:42.160
No doubt they started its cells growing them.

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:43.860
Alright, let's go.

00:22:45.130 --> 00:22:45.710
Come on, hurry up.

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:46.180
Wait.

00:22:46.280 --> 00:22:46.520
Shh.

00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:47.740
Thank you.

00:22:48.390 --> 00:22:48.810
Thank you.

00:22:56.620 --> 00:22:56.860
Another.

00:22:57.190 --> 00:22:58.810
I think we'd better report this to headquarters.

00:22:59.370 --> 00:22:59.810
Come on.

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:00.900
Thank you.

00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:02.280
Don't go so far.

00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:14.840
Line's broken.

00:23:24.060 --> 00:23:24.480
Tighten here!

00:24:02.680 --> 00:24:03.660
Thank you.

00:24:08.790 --> 00:24:09.190
Fucked up.

00:24:09.560 --> 00:24:10.860
Any idea what they're doing there?

00:24:12.150 --> 00:24:13.770
That spot sends out radio interference.

00:24:14.520 --> 00:24:15.260
Its source is right there.

00:24:16.150 --> 00:24:16.370
Thank you.

00:24:46.730 --> 00:24:47.410
Tremendous egg.

00:24:56.390 --> 00:24:57.450
The damage here is minimal.

00:24:58.280 --> 00:24:59.900
I estimate it'll take around 10 days.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.340
for us to get everything back in shape.

00:25:02.460 --> 00:25:03.560
And when the repairs are all...

00:25:03.560 --> 00:25:03.740
Doctor!

00:25:04.630 --> 00:25:05.570
I can't take it.

00:25:05.940 --> 00:25:06.800
I won't go on.

00:25:11.010 --> 00:25:13.030
Anybody who wants to quit, just raise your hands up.

00:25:16.660 --> 00:25:16.840
Doctor.

00:25:17.810 --> 00:25:18.850
You can't stop testing.

00:25:19.990 --> 00:25:22.150
You're not a member of this crew. You have no right to talk like that.

00:25:22.290 --> 00:25:25.070
I joined this crew. I've been working hard ever since the day I got here.

00:25:25.190 --> 00:25:25.610
You're nothing...

00:25:25.610 --> 00:25:26.030
Take it easy.

00:25:26.580 --> 00:25:28.280
It's stupid to start the fight, Furukawa.

00:25:28.890 --> 00:25:29.450
All of you.

00:25:30.500 --> 00:25:31.440
We can't leave the island.

00:25:32.710 --> 00:25:34.510
Our radio transmitter was knocked out by the heat.

00:25:35.240 --> 00:25:36.420
There's no way to call a ship here.

00:25:37.030 --> 00:25:38.350
You can fix the radio.

00:25:39.110 --> 00:25:41.010
I won't know until it's more thoroughly checked out.

